1. Global Anycast DNS with split-horizon
```
# /etc/named.conf (primary, 4 continents)
view "internal" {
    match-clients { 10.0.0.0/8; 2001:db8:fc00::/48; };
    zone "corp.example" { type master; file "internal/corp.example.zone"; };
};
view "external" {
    match-clients { any; };
    zone "corp.example" { type master; file "external/corp.example.zone"; };
};
```
The internal zone returns RFC-1918 addresses; external returns anycasted 1.1.1.0/24 space.  
Route health injection withdraws the prefix if the local node loses BGP to its upstream.

